Prerequisites
-------------

The following packages are needed

  - A C++26 compiler supporting reflection and contracts (GCC >= 16)
  - Meson (>= 1.4) and Ninja. Available at https://mesonbuild.com/
  - Boost (asio)
  - Gtkmm-4.0 (which itself needs GTK-4). Available at http://www.gtkmm.org/
  - The developer files of at least one of the supported databases:
    - MySQL (libmysqlclient) or MariaDB (Connector/C). Available via
      http://www.mysql.com/ or https://mariadb.org/
    - PostgreSQL (libpq). Available via https://www.postgresql.org/
    Every database found is built as module (installed in
    <libdir>/CDManager); the program uses the one of the database server
    it finds at runtime.
  - My YGP library; also availabe as a Sourceforge project
    (http://libymp.sourceforge.net/)
  - GNU gettext (for the translations)


How to build
------------

Inside the directory containing the source code type

  meson setup build [options]
  meson compile -C build
  meson install -C build

The options of an existing build directory can be changed with

  meson configure build [options]

(without options it lists all available options and their current values).


Common options
--------------

  --prefix=<path>               # default: /usr/local
  --buildtype=<type>            # debugoptimized (default), debug, release, ...
  -Dnls=disabled                # Disable national language support
  -Dactors=false                # To don't store actor-information
  -Dfilms=false                 # To not handle a certain type of media
  -Drecords=false
  -Dmysql=disabled              # Don't build the backend for MySQL/MariaDB
  -Dpostgresql=disabled         # Don't build the backend for PostgreSQL
                                # (enabled: Fail if the database isn't found;
                                # default auto: Build it, if found)
  -Dchecks=<level>              # Adds Checks and enforces the C++26 contracts
  -Dtrace=<level>               # Sets the tracelevel
  -Dtests=disabled              # Don't build the unit tests (they need Boost.Test)

If the database isn't found in a standard location, point pkg-config to it
(e.g. PKG_CONFIG_PATH=/opt/pgsql/lib/pkgconfig meson setup build) or put its
pg_config into the PATH.


Common targets
--------------

  meson test -C build                         # Runs the unit tests
  meson compile -C build CDManager-pot        # Updates po/CDManager.pot
  meson compile -C build CDManager-update-po  # Merges the .pot into the .po-files
  meson devenv -C build ./src/CDManager       # Runs the program uninstalled
  meson compile -C build createDB             # Creates the database
                                              # (createDB-mysql, if built
                                              # for both databases)
  meson compile -C build populateDB           # Fills the database with sample data
  meson dist -C build                         # Creates a source archive
  ninja -C build uninstall                    # Uninstalls (after you found out
                                              # what crap this package actually
                                              # contains)
